  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7560214a2c335bd4e9cc29951d82c1e3, type: 3}
  m_Name: Laruja
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NPCInfoSO
  npcID: senor_laruja
  displayName: "Se\xF1or Laruja"
  characterFullName: Laruja
  alias: None
  characterCategory: Civilian Guest
  portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 888204882d06bc64dac0d2a764ad1dca, type: 3}
  description: "A small civilian guest familiar with colonial society in the Philippines.
    He generally supports the opinions of Fray D\xE1maso and expresses prejudiced
    views about Filipinos"
  biography: "Se\xF1or Laruja is one of the civilians seated with Fray D\xE1maso,
    Fray Sibyla, Lieutenant Guevara and the newly arrived Blond Man. He is described
    as a very small man with a black beard and a noticeably large nose. When Fray
    D\xE1maso asks him to confirm his accusations against Filipinos, Laruja agrees
    with him. During dinner, he also questions Ibarra about his years abroad and
    his observations of European society."
  characterFacts:
  - His first name is not revealed.
  - He is described as very small.
  - He has a black beard.
  - He has a notably large nose.
  - He is already familiar with life in the Philippines.
  - "He supports Fray D\xE1maso\u2019s negative claims about Filipinos."
  introductionLines:
  - "Se\xF1or Laruja. I have spent enough time in this country to form a few opinions
    of my own."
  repeatDialogues:
  - lines:
    - Take care when contradicting Fray Damaso.
    - He does not enjoy being treated without proper deference.
